      Derived from the upstream flix.svg logo. Same terms as that logo.

At build or test time some tools fetch, include or patch the pinned upstream
checkout (legacy parity fixtures, Gazebo comparison plugin and model). That
material is not redistributed here and remains under upstream terms.

  adapters/crazyswarm2/ros/crazyflie_server.patch
      A patch against Crazyswarm2 (https://github.com/IMRCLab/crazyswarm2, pinned
      f1e09954f56cd08e7d9aff5e13dc9a68795914a3). Its context lines are Crazyswarm2
      code, Copyright the Crazyswarm2 authors, MIT licence. flix_sil.py and
      flix_backend.py are original work written against Crazyswarm2's interfaces.
      The Crazyswarm2 Docker image fetches Crazyswarm2 and the Crazyflie firmware
      (GPL-3.0, Bitcraze) at build time; neither is redistributed here.

Third-party Rust dependencies keep their own licences; `deny.toml` lists the
licences accepted for them.
